schema: "0.4"
id: sem-code-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-code
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-code>` element — a verbatim source
    listing with provenance chrome, rendered in the minimal-tech-light theme
    on a dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, muted
    #cbd5e1, border #334155, accent #60a5fa). The sheet shows FOUR stacked
    example cards, each a code listing inside a rounded 12px surface with a
    hairline border and a small mono uppercase caption above it.

    Every card keeps its listing byte-for-byte readable: monospace type,
    ~14px, tab-size 2, code glyphs in normal foreground over the surface —
    a listing is never dimmed, blurred or occluded.

    Card 1 — caption "DEFAULT (COPY)". A TypeScript listing titled with a
    filename caption "src/rotate.ts" and a small "TS" pill badge on a chrome
    strip above the code. Lines 2, 4 and 5 are MARKED: each carries a soft
    accent-blue tint behind the text at ~14% opacity (a low, even wash, no
    border), with the glyphs fully saturated and legible — a marker-pen
    emphasis, never a redaction. A single "Copy" control sits at the right
    end of the chrome strip. No Wrap control.

    Card 2 — caption "COPY + WRAP". The same listing and marks, but the
    chrome strip carries two controls, "Copy" and "Wrap". "Wrap" is
    unpressed (neutral hairline outline, muted label). A single very long
    line runs past the right edge with a thin, subtle horizontal scrollbar
    beneath it — the listing scrolls rather than folding.

    Card 3 — caption "WRAP ON". The same listing with "Wrap" pressed: its
    outline and label switch to the accent blue. The long line is soft-
    wrapped onto two lines inside the panel width; no horizontal scrollbar
    is visible.

    Card 4 — caption "JS-OFF / LANG-ONLY". A shell listing with no filename:
    the chrome strip carries only a small "SH" caption badge (mono,
    uppercase, muted, hairline underline) above the code, and no controls at
    all — the no-JavaScript state, where the language badge degrades to a
    plain caption. Nothing is interactive and nothing is hidden.

    Typography: clean system sans for captions (Inter-like), monospace for
    code, generous margins. Chrome is minimal — filename, one pill badge,
    small text buttons.
  negative: >
    occluded, dimmed, blurred or masked code lines; marked lines rendered as
    opaque blocks that hide glyphs; redaction bars; colored syntax-
    highlighting rainbow; neon glow; drop shadows on text; more than four
    cards; light background; watermark; lorem ipsum in the captions; invented
    buttons or toolbars beyond Copy and Wrap; a scrollbar drawn on the
    wrapped card.
  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155 borders, generous
    negative space. Looks like a panel from a design-system guide describing
    one component in its states.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-code/sem-code-enhanced-fixture-900.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-code/sem-code-nojs-fixture-900.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-code/sem-code-source-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-code-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: default
      label: "DEFAULT (COPY)"
      must_show:
        - a filename caption (src/rotate.ts) and one small "TS" pill badge
          on the chrome strip above the code
        - lines 2, 4 and 5 marked with a soft accent tint behind fully
          legible glyphs
        - a single Copy control at the right of the strip
      must_never:
        - occlude, dim, blur or bar any code line
        - render a marked line as an opaque block that hides glyphs
        - show a Wrap control
    - id: copy-wrap
      label: "COPY + WRAP"
      must_show:
        - both Copy and Wrap controls, Wrap unpressed (neutral outline)
        - one over-long line extending past the panel with a thin horizontal
          scrollbar beneath it
      must_never:
        - fold the long line (it scrolls, it does not wrap, until Wrap is on)
        - mark the Wrap control as active
    - id: wrap-on
      label: "WRAP ON"
      must_show:
        - the Wrap control pressed (accent-blue outline and label)
        - the long line soft-wrapped onto two lines inside the panel
      must_never:
        - draw a horizontal scrollbar on the wrapped card
        - clip or truncate the wrapped line
    - id: js-off
      label: "JS-OFF / LANG-ONLY"
      must_show:
        - a single "SH" mono uppercase caption badge above the code
        - no controls of any kind
      must_never:
        - show Copy/Wrap controls in the no-JavaScript state
        - hide or dim the listing

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    marked-line-legibility:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        Marked lines read as an even accent wash behind normal-contrast
        glyphs; the code stays the most legible thing on the card.
      fail_signals:
        - marked line occluded, blurred or low-contrast
        - opaque filled block over the marked line
        - marked line restyled beyond the tint (italic, strike, colour swap)
    chrome-fidelity:
      weight: 0.3
      description: >
        The chrome strip carries exactly the controls each mode defines —
        filename plus one lang badge, and Copy and/or Wrap — with Wrap's
        pressed state set by the mode.
      fail_signals:
        - Wrap shown on the default or JS-off card
        - Wrap pressed on the copy+wrap card
        - invented buttons, tabs or toolbars beyond Copy and Wrap
    wrap-and-overflow:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        copy+wrap shows a long line with a horizontal scrollbar; wrap-on
        shows the same line soft-wrapped with no scrollbar.
      fail_signals:
        - scrollbar drawn on the wrapped card
        - wrapped card clips the line
        - both wrap cards identical
    spec-sheet-quality:
      weight: 0.15
      description: >
        Reads as a component design sheet: four labeled cards, consistent
        monospace listings, dark minimal-tech palette, no decorative noise.
      fail_signals:
        - watermark, lorem ipsum, rainbow syntax colouring
        - more or fewer than four labeled cards
  reject_if:
    - any card occludes, bars or blurs a code line
    - the JS-off card shows interactive controls